# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefill window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefill-1 and push a tag
# experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch that holds them. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the classes, the minutes, the read rules and the NO-GO rules. Push ONE tag at a time and wait for its run to finish (the workflow keeps one pending run; queued tags are cancelled). Never cancel a running card job.
# PP1 (SOFT): the PREFILL DEVICE OP PROFILE of real 2,048-token Lever N prefill chunks at every context, on the production profile, image tp4-next2-1 (the integrated tp4/next-2 image: its graft carries the layer.py
# profiler-flush hook, inert unless its switch is set). Gate plans ops-prefill-twin then ops-prefill-trace (scripts/ci/ops_profile_plan.py, docs/tp4-profile.md 'Prefill profile'): ONE user and ONE real-text coding prompt of
# 131,072 tokens = 64 prefill chunks (chunk 0 is the short context, chunk 63 the long one, so one prompt gives every context), an 8-token answer, ignore_eos.
#   ops-prefill-twin   unprofiled: the prefill wall time per chunk the profiled arm is compared with (the perturbation reference) and the answer text (the text reference).
#   ops-prefill-trace  profiled: tracy at op-support 20000 (the only count the plan accepts: 200000 segfaulted the dispatch thread three times), the CPP post-process only (no raw device log), and
#                      QWEN_PREFILL_PROFILE_FLUSH=1: the hook drains the device profiler every 16 decoder layers of a prefill forward, so no chunk overflows the per-core buffers (the TP2 prefill profile lost rows
#                      after about layer 22 of ONE chunk without it).
# NEVER CANCEL this job once its gate step has started: the profiler writes as root, and a cancelled run leaves root-owned logs, so the next checkout dies with EACCES (the workflow's always() hand-back step keeps the
# compressed CPP report and prunes, but a killed container can still be writing). A segfault in read_core_data_from_completion_queue is INFRA: do not raise op-support. Disk: the gate refuses to start past 80 percent used and the guard
# stops the arm at 4 GB of profile output or 85 percent; never delete the base image the build starts from (grep the Dockerfiles for FROM before deleting any image). The profiled arm reserves about 0.7 GB of device DRAM per chip
# on top of the eight-seat 262k pool: an attach refusal there is a finding (rerun on a smaller pool), not a bug in the plan.
# READ the artifact's gate/ops/prefill-profile-report.md (and .json; the compressed CPP report is cpp_device_perf_report.prefill.csv.gz; to rerun the analysis: python3 scripts/ci/tp4_prefill_profile_report.py
# --help): VALIDITY first (the launched argv has QWEN_FAST_TP=4, both verify audits 0, the profiler variables and QWEN_PREFILL_PROFILE_FLUSH=1; the '[PINDIAG] prefill profile flush' marker lines are in the server log; the report
# found 64 chunks on every chip with equal row counts; no dropped-marker line), then per chunk: weight matmuls with achieved TFLOP/s and the share of the stated peak (an ESTIMATE), attention prefill against context (fixed cost +
# slope per 1k tokens), the GDN chunked prefill (conv calls per chunk and per GDN layer), glue and layout copies, norms, collectives (calls per chunk, ms per call, minimum over chips and skew). The flush hook has NEVER run at TP4
# or at op-support 20000, and the report has never seen a real TP4 prefill CSV: both arms are DATA, not a gate (SOFT). The ops-prefill-trace text is held against the twin's; a difference is reported FAIL to look at (profiling
# shifts scheduling), the numbers are still read.
# NOT TIMED: attribution only (CI need not be paused). Duration (estimate): status 2 + reset and heal 5, ops-prefill-twin 20 (worst case 105), ops-prefill-trace 80 (a cold JIT of every profiler-define kernel, 64 chunks
# x 4 flushes, the close; worst case 135), about 120 minutes in all (worst case 255); the box is 300.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=status reset gate
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-traffic
C2_GATE_PLAN=ops-prefill-twin,ops-prefill-trace
C2_GATE_JIT=record
C2_BOX_MINUTES=300
